   "text": {
    "L1": "Saving means keeping some money aside for later.",
    "L2": "We may save for something bigger, emergencies, or the future.",
    "L3": "We can save in a gullak, a bank account, or a post office savings account.",
    "L4": "A gullak keeps money at home, but it can be lost or broken and it does not grow.",
    "L5": "In a bank, money is recorded in our account, not kept as our exact notes.",
    "L6": "The bank uses money from many savers to give loans and pays savers a little interest.",
    "L7": "When we withdraw, we get the same amount plus interest, not necessarily the same notes.",
    "L8": "Anu saves ₹40 minus ₹10, so she saves ₹30 each week.",
    "L9": "To reach ₹240, she needs 8 weeks because 8 times ₹30 equals ₹240."
   },
